The EVENT LOG behind samples/drive_dsh.live-redacted.out -- the artefact that file's own
summary line `"notifications": 16` is a claim about.

It is here because a review made the right point about that summary: instruments/drive_dsh.py's
docstring promises "every server notification is written verbatim to --events, so 'it ran' is an
artefact a reader can count rather than a verdict this file asserts" -- and the events file was
not committed, so the only evidence for the run WAS the asserted verdict. Now it can be counted.

Not reproducible: it is one live dsh turn against a stub upstream, on node v24.21.0, from a
throwaway DSH_HOME. The session id is the one this run chose (ari28-J), matching that sample.

REDACTED, and every substitution is the SAME BYTE LENGTH as what it replaced, so no figure
derived from this file can shift: this box's capture working directory, and 4 of dsh's own
per-message UUIDs, which become `redacted-identifier-NNN` padded to a UUID's 36 characters --
the same convention samples/fixtures/request_construction.dsh.jsonl already uses, so the two
files read alike. No credential appears: the run's DEEPSEEK_API_KEY placeholder is assembled at
runtime, never reaches the rail, and a grep for it here returns nothing.

What the 16 notifications are, counted from the lines below:
   2  session.event:agent/inbox/spliced
   1  session.event:assistant/message
   1  session.event:request/context
   1  session.event:request/header
   1  session.event:session-log-deepseek/delivery-accepted
   1  session.event:session/title
   1  session.event:step/end
   1  session.event:step/start
   1  session.event:system/message
   1  session.event:turn/end
   1  session.event:turn/start
   2  session.event:user/message
   2  session.status:-
  Six independent runs of this same turn each produced exactly 16 notifications of this same
  shape, which is why the count is quoted as a property of the turn and not of one run.

